# Machine-local CLI state, written by `supabase link`. It holds this machine's
# resolved project ref, the pooler URL and the remote service versions - none of
# it belongs in the repo, and it is regenerated by one command.
#
# 🔴 On some CLI versions `.temp/pooler-url` carries the DATABASE PASSWORD inline.
# It does not on 2.107.0 (checked 2026-09-07), which is precisely why this rule is
# not conditional on that: the next version is not required to keep it out.
.temp/

# 🔴 NOT ignored, deliberately: `config.toml`. Nothing creates one here today -
# `supabase link` did not - and this project is hosted-only, so a config.toml full
# of 127.0.0.1 ports would be leftover scaffolding worth SEEING in a diff rather
# than hiding. An over-broad ignore rule is what kept `desktop/.env.example` out
# of this repo entirely; one instance of that per project is enough.
